IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part I, "Payment of Benefits": ss 12, 13 and 13.1. Layer 1 of piece ei1.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30.
-- This module comes BEFORE ei1-benefit-period.l4 in the import order, because s 10(13) to (15) call s 12(3);
-- the two places where s 12 reads s 10 (s 12(5) and s 12(7)) take the figures as plain inputs, so nothing here
-- imports ei1-benefit-period.l4.

§ `Section 12(1) - benefits for each week of unemployment`

-- src:332 | 12 (1) If a benefit period has been established for a claimant, benefits may be paid to the claimant for each week of unemployment that falls in the benefit period, subject to the maximums established by this section.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(1) (src:332)
GIVEN `a benefit period has been established for the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week is a week of unemployment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week falls in the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 12(1) benefits may be paid to the claimant for the week` IF
        `a benefit period has been established for the claimant`
    AND `the week is a week of unemployment`
    AND `the week falls in the benefit period`

§ `Section 12(2) to (2.5) - the general maximum`

-- src:334 | (2) The maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period because of a reason other than those mentioned in subsection (3) shall be determined in accordance with the table in Schedule I by reference to the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant and the number of hours of insurable employment of the claimant in their qualifying period.
-- The table in Schedule I is piece ei6's: the figure it gives for the rate and the hours is an input.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(2) (src:334)
GIVEN -- out of range: Schedule I (piece ei6)
      `the maximum number of weeks in the table in Schedule I for the regional rate of unemployment and the hours of insurable employment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 12(2) the general maximum number of weeks for a reason other than those mentioned in subsection (3)` IS
    `the maximum number of weeks in the table in Schedule I for the regional rate of unemployment and the hours of insurable employment`

-- src:336 | (2.1) Despite subsection (2), the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period because of a reason other than those mentioned in subsection (3) to a claimant whose benefit period begins during the period beginning on September 27, 2020 and ending on September 25, 2021 is 50.
-- src:337 | Non-application
-- src:338 | (2.2) Subsection (2.1) does not apply to a claimant under the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations.
-- Dates stated by the text, carried as data: 27 September 2020 to 25 September 2021.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(2.1) (src:336)
`s 12(2.1) the period within which a benefit period must begin for the maximum to be 50 weeks` MEANS
    `Period of days` OF (YMD 2020 9 27), (YMD 2021 9 25)

@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(2.1), s 12(2.2) (src:336) (src:338)
GIVEN `the day on which the claimant's benefit period begins` IS A DATE
      `the claimant is a claimant under the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 12(2.1) the maximum number of weeks is 50 for a benefit period that begins during the period` IF
        `the day` `the day on which the claimant's benefit period begins` `falls within` `s 12(2.1) the period within which a benefit period must begin for the maximum to be 50 weeks`
    AND NOT (`the claimant is a claimant under the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations`)

-- src:336 | (2.1) Despite subsection (2), the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period because of a reason other than those mentioned in subsection (3) to a claimant whose benefit period begins during the period beginning on September 27, 2020 and ending on September 25, 2021 is 50.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(2.1) (src:336)
`s 12(2.1) the maximum number of weeks for a benefit period that begins during that period` MEANS 50

-- src:342 | (i) the date on which a benefit period for the claimant is established falls within the period beginning on September 26, 2021 and ending on October 7, 2028,
-- The period within which the benefit period must be established: 26 September 2021 to 7 October 2028.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(2.3)(a)(i) (src:342)
`s 12(2.3)(a)(i) the period within which a benefit period must be established` MEANS
    `Period of days` OF (YMD 2021 9 26), (YMD 2028 10 7)

-- An earlier benefit period of the claimant, as the seasonal-worker test reads it: the day it began (a Sunday), whether
-- regular benefits were paid or payable during it, and whether the claimant received a notification of payment or
-- non-payment for a week within the 260 weeks (s 12(2.4)). "Established" in s 12(2.3)(a)(iii) is read as "began":
-- the Act dates an earlier benefit period by the week it begins (fork F-established in NOTES.md).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(2.3), s 12(2.4) (src:344) (src:348)
DECLARE `ei1 Earlier benefit period` HAS
    `ei1 the first day of the earlier benefit period`                                                  IS A DATE
    `ei1 regular benefits were paid or payable during the earlier benefit period`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `ei1 the claimant received a notification of payment or non-payment for a week within the 260 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:348 | (2.4) For the purposes of subparagraph (2.3)(a)(iii), a claimant’s benefit period established before the beginning of the 260-week period is considered to have been established within the 260-week period if the claimant received a notification of payment or non-payment with respect to any week that falls within that 260-week period.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(2.4) (src:348)
GIVEN earlier IS A `ei1 Earlier benefit period`
      `the first day of the benefit period referred to in subparagraph (2.3)(a)(i)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 12(2.4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have been established within the 260 weeks` IF
        (`the day` (earlier's `ei1 the first day of the earlier benefit period`) `falls within`
            (`Period of days` OF (`the first day of the benefit period referred to in subparagraph (2.3)(a)(i)` MINUS `weeks as days` 260), (`the first day of the benefit period referred to in subparagraph (2.3)(a)(i)` MINUS 1)))
     OR (    earlier's `ei1 the first day of the earlier benefit period` BELOW (`the first day of the benefit period referred to in subparagraph (2.3)(a)(i)` MINUS `weeks as days` 260)
         AND earlier's `ei1 the claimant received a notification of payment or non-payment for a week within the 260 weeks`)

-- src:350 | (2.5) For the purposes of subparagraph (2.3)(a)(iv), a benefit period in a previous year is considered to have begun around the same time of year if it began during the period that begins eight weeks before and ends eight weeks after the week that is
-- src:351 | (a) 52 weeks before the first week of the benefit period referred to in subparagraph (2.3)(a)(i);
-- src:352 | (b) 104 weeks before the first week of the benefit period referred to in subparagraph (2.3)(a)(i);
-- src:353 | (c) 156 weeks before the first week of the benefit period referred to in subparagraph (2.3)(a)(i);
-- src:354 | (d) 208 weeks before the first week of the benefit period referred to in subparagraph (2.3)(a)(i); or
-- src:355 | (e) 260 weeks before the first week of the benefit period referred to in subparagraph (2.3)(a)(i).
-- "Around the same time of year": it began during the period that begins eight weeks before and ends eight weeks
-- after the week that is 52, 104, 156, 208 or 260 weeks before the first week of the current benefit period. Read as
-- running from the first day of the week eight weeks before to the last day of the week eight weeks after
-- (fork F-around in NOTES.md). The helper takes one of the five weeks (n times 52 weeks before).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(2.5) (src:350-355)
GIVEN `the day on which the earlier benefit period began` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the benefit period referred to in subparagraph (2.3)(a)(i)` IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 12(2.5) the earlier benefit period began during the period around the week that is n times 52 weeks before` IF
    `the day` `the day on which the earlier benefit period began` `falls within` `the period` 
    WHERE
        `the week that is n times 52 weeks before` MEANS
            `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` (`the first day of the benefit period referred to in subparagraph (2.3)(a)(i)` MINUS `weeks as days` (52 TIMES n))
        `the period` MEANS
            `Period of days` OF (`the week that is n times 52 weeks before` MINUS `weeks as days` 8), (`s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` (`the week that is n times 52 weeks before` PLUS `weeks as days` 8))

@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(2.5) (src:350-355)
GIVEN `the day on which the earlier benefit period began` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the benefit period referred to in subparagraph (2.3)(a)(i)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 12(2.5) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` IF
    any (GIVEN n YIELD `s 12(2.5) the earlier benefit period began during the period around the week that is n times 52 weeks before` `the day on which the earlier benefit period began` `the first day of the benefit period referred to in subparagraph (2.3)(a)(i)` n)
        (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5)

-- src:340 | (2.3) Despite subsection (2), the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period to a claimant because of a reason other than those mentioned in subsection (3) shall be determined in accordance with the table set out in Schedule V by reference to the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant and the number of hours of insurable employment of the claimant in their qualifying period if
-- src:341 | (a) the following conditions are met:
-- src:342 | (i) the date on which a benefit period for the claimant is established falls within the period beginning on September 26, 2021 and ending on October 7, 2028,
-- src:343 | (ii) on the date on which the benefit period is established, the claimant is ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule VI,
-- src:344 | (iii) in the 260 weeks before the date on which the benefit period referred to in subparagraph (i) begins, at least three benefit periods were established during which regular benefits were paid or payable, and
-- src:345 | (iv) at least two of the benefit periods referred to in subparagraph (iii) began around the same time of year as the benefit period referred to in subparagraph (i) began; or
-- src:346 | (b) the conditions referred to in subparagraphs (a)(i) and (ii) are met and the claimant had met the criteria set out in paragraphs 77.992(2)(b) to (d) of the Employment Insurance Regulations — taking into account subsections 77.992(3) and (4) of those Regulations — in respect of a benefit period established for the claimant on a date within the period referred to in paragraph 77.992(2)(a) of those Regulations.
-- The seasonal-worker test. The caller passes the claimant's earlier benefit periods; the test counts those that
-- fall in the 260 weeks (iii) and, among them, those that began around the same time of year (iv). Paragraph (b)
-- is an alternative: conditions (a)(i) and (a)(ii) and the claimant's having met the criteria in reg 77.992(2)(b)
-- to (d) (piece er5), which is an input. The region in Schedule VI (piece ei6) is an input.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(2.3) (src:340-346)
GIVEN `the day on which the benefit period for the claimant is established` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the benefit period referred to in subparagraph (2.3)(a)(i)` IS A DATE
      -- out of range: Schedule VI (piece ei6)
      `on the date on which the benefit period is established, the claimant is ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule VI` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's earlier benefit periods` IS A LIST OF `ei1 Earlier benefit period`
      -- out of range: reg 77.992(2)(b) to (d), (3) and (4) (piece er5)
      `the claimant had met the criteria set out in paragraphs 77.992(2)(b) to (d) of the Employment Insurance Regulations in respect of a benefit period established within the period referred to in paragraph 77.992(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks is read from the table in Schedule V` IF
        (   `s 12(2.3)(a)(i) and (ii) are met`
         AND (   `s 12(2.3)(a)(iii) and (iv) are met`
              OR `the claimant had met the criteria set out in paragraphs 77.992(2)(b) to (d) of the Employment Insurance Regulations in respect of a benefit period established within the period referred to in paragraph 77.992(2)(a)`))
    WHERE
        `s 12(2.3)(a)(i) and (ii) are met` MEANS
                (`the day` `the day on which the benefit period for the claimant is established` `falls within` `s 12(2.3)(a)(i) the period within which a benefit period must be established`)
            AND `on the date on which the benefit period is established, the claimant is ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule VI`
        `those established within the 260 weeks` MEANS
            filter (GIVEN e YIELD e's `ei1 regular benefits were paid or payable during the earlier benefit period`
                              AND `s 12(2.4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have been established within the 260 weeks` e `the first day of the benefit period referred to in subparagraph (2.3)(a)(i)`)
                   `the claimant's earlier benefit periods`
        `s 12(2.3)(a)(iii) and (iv) are met` MEANS
                count `those established within the 260 weeks` AT LEAST 3
            AND count (filter (GIVEN e YIELD `s 12(2.5) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (e's `ei1 the first day of the earlier benefit period`) `the first day of the benefit period referred to in subparagraph (2.3)(a)(i)`)
                              `those established within the 260 weeks`) AT LEAST 2

-- The maximum for the benefit period under the general rule, before the special benefits of subsection (3):
-- subsection (2.3) is tested first, then (2.1); fork F-overlap in NOTES.md says why the order cannot matter on the
-- dates the text fixes.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(2), s 12(2.1), s 12(2.3) (src:334) (src:336) (src:340)
GIVEN `the maximum number of weeks in the table in Schedule I for the regional rate of unemployment and the hours of insurable employment` IS A NUMBER
      -- out of range: Schedule V (piece ei6)
      `the maximum number of weeks in the table in Schedule V for the regional rate of unemployment and the hours of insurable employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum number of weeks is 50 for a benefit period that begins during the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum number of weeks is read from the table in Schedule V` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 12(2), s 12(2.1) and s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks for a reason other than those mentioned in subsection (3)` IS
    BRANCH IF `the maximum number of weeks is read from the table in Schedule V` THEN `the maximum number of weeks in the table in Schedule V for the regional rate of unemployment and the hours of insurable employment`
           IF `the maximum number of weeks is 50 for a benefit period that begins during the period` THEN `s 12(2.1) the maximum number of weeks for a benefit period that begins during that period`
           OTHERWISE `s 12(2) the general maximum number of weeks for a reason other than those mentioned in subsection (3)` `the maximum number of weeks in the table in Schedule I for the regional rate of unemployment and the hours of insurable employment`

-- s 12(2.6) to (2.8): [Repealed, 2016, c. 7, s. 212] (src line 356). Nothing to encode.

§ `Section 12(3) to (4.5) - special benefits`

-- src:358 | (3) The maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period
-- src:359 | (a) because of pregnancy is 15;
-- src:360 | (b) because the claimant is caring for one or more new-born children of the claimant or one or more children placed with the claimant for the purpose of adoption is, in accordance with the election under section 23,
-- src:361 | (i) 35, or
-- src:362 | (ii) 61;
-- src:363 | (c) because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine is 26;
-- src:364 | (d) because the claimant is providing care or support to one or more family members described in subsection 23.1(2) is 26;
-- src:365 | (e) because the claimant is providing care or support to one or more critically ill children described in subsection 23.2(1), is 35; and
-- src:366 | (f) because the claimant is providing care or support to one or more critically ill adults described in subsection 23.3(1) is 15.
-- The maximum number of weeks for a reason in (3). For caring for a new-born or adopted child the figure follows the
-- election under section 23 (35 or 61). NOTHING for "a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)", whose
-- maximum is the general maximum of subsection (2).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(3) (src:358-366)
GIVEN reason IS A `Reason for benefits`
      election IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 12(3) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period for the reason` IS
    CONSIDER reason
    WHEN `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `pregnancy`                                               THEN JUST 15
    WHEN `caring for a new-born or adopted child`                  THEN JUST (IF election EQUALS `the 35-week maximum` THEN 35 ELSE 61)
    WHEN `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine`              THEN JUST 26
    WHEN `care or support of a family member`                      THEN JUST 26
    WHEN `care or support of a critically ill child`               THEN JUST 35
    WHEN `care or support of a critically ill adult`               THEN JUST 15

-- src:369 | (a) for a single pregnancy is 15; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(4)(a) (src:369)
`s 12(4)(a) the maximum number of weeks for a single pregnancy` MEANS 15

-- src:370 | (b) for the care of one or more new-born or adopted children as a result of a single pregnancy or placement is,
-- src:371 | (i) if the maximum number of weeks that has been elected under subsection 23(1.1) is established under subparagraph (3)(b)(i), 35 or, if the weeks for which benefits may be paid are divided in accordance with section 23, 40, or
-- src:372 | (ii) if the maximum number of weeks that has been elected under subsection 23(1.1) is established under subparagraph (3)(b)(ii), 61 or, if the weeks for which benefits may be paid are divided in accordance with section 23, 69.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(4)(b) (src:370-372)
GIVEN election IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
      `the weeks for which benefits may be paid are divided in accordance with section 23` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 12(4)(b) the maximum number of weeks for the care of one or more new-born or adopted children as a result of a single pregnancy or placement` IS
    CONSIDER election
    WHEN `the 35-week maximum` THEN IF `the weeks for which benefits may be paid are divided in accordance with section 23` THEN 40 ELSE 35
    WHEN `the 61-week maximum` THEN IF `the weeks for which benefits may be paid are divided in accordance with section 23` THEN 69 ELSE 61

-- src:374 | (4.01) If a claim is made under this Part in respect of a child or children referred to in paragraph (4)(b) and a claim is made under section 152.05 in respect of the same child or children, the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable under this Act in respect of the child or children is,
-- src:375 | (a) if the maximum number of weeks that has been elected under subsection 23(1.1) is established under subparagraph (3)(b)(i), 35 or, if the weeks for which benefits may be paid are divided in accordance with section 23, 40; or
-- src:376 | (b) if the maximum number of weeks that has been elected under subsection 23(1.1) is established under subparagraph (3)(b)(ii), 61 or, if the weeks for which benefits may be paid are divided in accordance with section 23, 69.
-- Where claims are made in respect of the same child or children under this Part and under section 152.05 (Part VII.1,
-- piece ei5), the maximum under the Act as a whole is the same figure as in paragraph (4)(b).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(4.01) (src:374-376)
GIVEN `a claim is made under this Part in respect of the child or children referred to in paragraph (4)(b) and a claim is made under section 152.05 in respect of the same child or children` IS A BOOLEAN
      election IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
      `the weeks for which benefits may be paid are divided in accordance with section 23` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 12(4.01) the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable under the Act in respect of the child or children` IS
    IF `a claim is made under this Part in respect of the child or children referred to in paragraph (4)(b) and a claim is made under section 152.05 in respect of the same child or children`
    THEN JUST (`s 12(4)(b) the maximum number of weeks for the care of one or more new-born or adopted children as a result of a single pregnancy or placement` election `the weeks for which benefits may be paid are divided in accordance with section 23`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:378 | (4.1) Even if more than one claim is made under this Act, at least one of which is made under section 23.1 — or even if more than one certificate is issued for the purposes of this Act, at least one of which is issued for the purposes of section 23.1 — for the same reason and in respect of the same family member, the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable under this Act in respect of that family member is 26 weeks during the period of 52 weeks that begins on the first day of the week referred to in paragraph 23.1(4)(a).
-- The 26 weeks are shared by every claim made for the same reason about the same family member, under this Act as a
-- whole. The input is the weeks already paid under every such claim during the 52 weeks (or the shorter period of
-- subsection (4.2)).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(4.1) (src:378)
`s 12(4.1) the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable in respect of the family member` MEANS 26

@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(4.1) (src:378)
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits already paid or payable under this Act in respect of that family member during the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 12(4.1) the weeks of benefits still payable in respect of the family member` IS
    max 0 (`s 12(4.1) the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable in respect of the family member` MINUS `the weeks of benefits already paid or payable under this Act in respect of that family member during the period`)

-- src:380 | (4.2) If a shorter period is prescribed for the purposes of subsection 23.1(5), then that shorter period applies for the purposes of subsection (4.1).
-- The shorter period is prescribed for the purposes of subsection 23.1(5). No regulation in the deposited
-- Regulations (current to 2026-09-30) names one, so the length is an input that is NOTHING when none is prescribed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(4.2) (src:380)
GIVEN `the length in weeks of the shorter period prescribed for the purposes of subsection 23.1(5), if one is prescribed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 12(4.2) the length in weeks of the period of 52 weeks in subsection (4.1), or of the shorter period if one is prescribed` IS
    CONSIDER `the length in weeks of the shorter period prescribed for the purposes of subsection 23.1(5), if one is prescribed`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 52
    WHEN JUST shorter THEN shorter

-- src:382 | (4.3) When a shorter period referred to in subsection (4.2) has expired in respect of a family member, no further benefits are payable under section 23.1 in respect of that family member until the minimum prescribed number of weeks has elapsed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(4.3) (src:382)
GIVEN `a shorter period referred to in subsection (4.2) has expired in respect of the family member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minimum prescribed number of weeks has elapsed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 12(4.3) further benefits are payable under section 23.1 in respect of the family member` IF
        NOT (`a shorter period referred to in subsection (4.2) has expired in respect of the family member`)
     OR `the minimum prescribed number of weeks has elapsed`

-- src:384 | (4.4) Even if more than one claim is made under this Act, at least one of which is made under section 23.2 — or even if more than one certificate is issued for the purposes of this Act, at least one of which is issued for the purposes of section 23.2 — for the same reason and in respect of the same critically ill child, the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable under this Act in respect of that child is 35 weeks during the period of 52 weeks that begins on the first day of the week referred to in paragraph 23.2(3)(a).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(4.4) (src:384)
`s 12(4.4) the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable in respect of the critically ill child` MEANS 35

@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(4.4) (src:384)
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits already paid or payable under this Act in respect of that child during the period of 52 weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 12(4.4) the weeks of benefits still payable in respect of the critically ill child` IS
    max 0 (`s 12(4.4) the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable in respect of the critically ill child` MINUS `the weeks of benefits already paid or payable under this Act in respect of that child during the period of 52 weeks`)

-- src:386 | (4.5) Even if more than one claim is made under this Act, at least one of which is made under section 23.3 — or even if more than one certificate is issued for the purposes of this Act, at least one of which is issued for the purposes of section 23.3 — for the same reason and in respect of the same critically ill adult, the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable under this Act in respect of that adult is 15 weeks during the period of 52 weeks that begins on the first day of the week referred to in paragraph 23.3(3)(a).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(4.5) (src:386)
`s 12(4.5) the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable in respect of the critically ill adult` MEANS 15

@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(4.5) (src:386)
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits already paid or payable under this Act in respect of that adult during the period of 52 weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 12(4.5) the weeks of benefits still payable in respect of the critically ill adult` IS
    max 0 (`s 12(4.5) the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable in respect of the critically ill adult` MINUS `the weeks of benefits already paid or payable under this Act in respect of that adult during the period of 52 weeks`)

§ `Section 12(5) to (8) - combined weeks`

-- src:388 | (5) In a claimant’s benefit period, the claimant may combine weeks of benefits to which they are entitled because of a reason mentioned in subsection (3), but the maximum number of combined weeks is 50. If the benefit period is extended under subsection 10(13), the maximum number of combined weeks equals the maximum number of weeks in the benefit period calculated under subsection 10(15) less two weeks.
-- If the benefit period is extended under s 10(13), the maximum is the length of the benefit period calculated under
-- s 10(15) less two weeks; otherwise 50. The s 10(15) figure comes from ei1-benefit-period.l4 and is passed in.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(5) (src:388)
GIVEN `the benefit period is extended under subsection 10(13)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum number of weeks in the benefit period calculated under subsection 10(15)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 12(5) the maximum number of combined weeks of benefits because of reasons mentioned in subsection (3)` IS
    IF `the benefit period is extended under subsection 10(13)`
    THEN `the maximum number of weeks in the benefit period calculated under subsection 10(15)` MINUS 2
    ELSE 50

-- src:390 | (6) In a claimant’s benefit period, the claimant may, subject to the applicable maximums, combine weeks of benefits to which the claimant is entitled under subsection (2), (2.1) or (2.3) and because of a reason mentioned in subsection (3), but the total number of weeks of benefits shall not exceed 50.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(6) (src:390)
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits to which the claimant is entitled under subsection (2), (2.1) or (2.3)` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of benefits to which the claimant is entitled because of a reason mentioned in subsection (3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 12(6) the total number of weeks of benefits that may be combined` IS
    min 50 (`the weeks of benefits to which the claimant is entitled under subsection (2), (2.1) or (2.3)` PLUS `the weeks of benefits to which the claimant is entitled because of a reason mentioned in subsection (3)`)

-- src:392 | (7) For the purpose of determining whether the total number of weeks of benefits established under subsection (6) has been reached, in the case where benefits have been paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b) and the applicable maximum number of weeks is established under subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii),
-- src:393 | (a) the number of weeks of benefits that were paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b) is converted to the number of weeks of benefits that would have been paid at a rate of weekly benefits of 55%, as set out in the table in Schedule IV; and
-- src:394 | (b) other than the weeks referred to in subsections 10(10) to (12.1) in respect of which the benefit period is extended and the week referred to in section 13, the weeks for which no benefits were paid are deemed to be weeks for which benefits were paid at a rate of weekly benefits of 55%.
-- (a) weeks paid for the reason in paragraph 12(3)(b) at the 61-week maximum are converted to weeks at 55% by the
-- table in Schedule IV (piece ei6; the converted figure is an input). (b) weeks for which no benefits were paid are
-- deemed paid at 55%, except the weeks of the extensions in 10(10) to (12.1) and the waiting-period week.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(7) (src:392-394)
GIVEN -- out of range: Schedule IV (piece ei6)
      `the number of weeks of benefits paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b) converted to weeks at a rate of weekly benefits of 55%, as set out in the table in Schedule IV` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks of other benefits paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks of the benefit period for which no benefits were paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks in respect of which the benefit period is extended under subsections 10(10) to (12.1)` IS A NUMBER
      `the week referred to in section 13 is among the weeks for which no benefits were paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 12(7) the number of weeks that count toward the total number of weeks of benefits established under subsection (6)` IS
    `the number of weeks of benefits paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b) converted to weeks at a rate of weekly benefits of 55%, as set out in the table in Schedule IV`
    PLUS `the number of weeks of other benefits paid`
    PLUS max 0 (`the number of weeks of the benefit period for which no benefits were paid`
                MINUS `the number of weeks in respect of which the benefit period is extended under subsections 10(10) to (12.1)`
                MINUS (IF `the week referred to in section 13 is among the weeks for which no benefits were paid` THEN 1 ELSE 0))

-- src:396 | (8) For the purposes of this section, the placement with a major attachment claimant, at the same or substantially the same time, of two or more children for the purpose of adoption is a single placement of a child or children for the purpose of adoption.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 12(8) (src:396)
GIVEN `two or more children are placed with a major attachment claimant for the purpose of adoption at the same or substantially the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 12(8) the placement is a single placement of a child or children for the purpose of adoption` IF
    `two or more children are placed with a major attachment claimant for the purpose of adoption at the same or substantially the same time`

§ `Section 13 - the waiting period`

-- src:398 | 13 A claimant is not entitled to be paid benefits in a benefit period until, after the beginning of the benefit period, the claimant has served a waiting period of one week of unemployment for which benefits would otherwise be payable.
-- The waiting period is "the one week of the benefit period described in section 13" (s 6(1)).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 13 (src:398)
GIVEN `the number of weeks of unemployment for which benefits would otherwise be payable that the claimant has served as a waiting period since the beginning of the benefit period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 13 the claimant has served a waiting period of one week of unemployment` IF
    `the number of weeks of unemployment for which benefits would otherwise be payable that the claimant has served as a waiting period since the beginning of the benefit period` AT LEAST 1

@ref Employment Insurance Act s 13 (src:398)
GIVEN `the claimant has served a waiting period of one week of unemployment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 13 the claimant is entitled to be paid benefits in the benefit period` IF
    `the claimant has served a waiting period of one week of unemployment`

§ `Section 13.1 - a week deemed to be a week for which benefits would otherwise be payable`

-- src:400 | 13.1 (1) For the purpose of determining a claimant’s waiting period, a week of unemployment is deemed to be a week of unemployment for which benefits would otherwise be payable if — were the week not the waiting period — the amount of the benefits that would have been payable in that week after deducting the following would be greater than zero:
-- src:401 | (a) the amount of the earnings, if any, that is greater than $50, if the claimant’s rate of weekly benefits is less than $200; or
-- src:402 | (b) the amount of the earnings, if any, that is greater than 25% of the claimant’s rate of weekly benefits, if that rate is $200 or more.
-- src:403 | References
-- src:404 | (2) For the purpose of subsection (1),
-- src:405 | (a) in determining the amount of the benefits that would have been payable, the deduction referred to in subsection 19(2) is to be excluded; and
-- src:406 | (b) a reference to earnings means earnings as determined for the purpose of subsection 19(2).
-- "Were the week not the waiting period": the benefits that week would carry are the rate of weekly benefits, less
-- the earnings above $50 (rate under $200) or above 25% of the rate (rate of $200 or more), and the week counts if
-- that is greater than zero. The 19(2) deduction is left out (s 13.1(2)(a)) and "earnings" are those of s 19(2)
-- (s 13.1(2)(b)). The 25% of the rate is rounded under s 6(2).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 13.1(1), s 13.1(2) (src:400-402) (src:404-406)
GIVEN `the claimant's rate of weekly benefits` IS A NUMBER
      `the earnings of the claimant in the week, as determined for the purpose of subsection 19(2)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 13.1(1) the week of unemployment is deemed to be a week of unemployment for which benefits would otherwise be payable` IF
    `the claimant's rate of weekly benefits` MINUS `the amount of the earnings, if any, that is greater than the threshold` GREATER THAN 0
    WHERE
        `the threshold` MEANS
            IF `the claimant's rate of weekly benefits` BELOW 200
            THEN 50
            ELSE `s 6(2) and s 152.01(5) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` (`the claimant's rate of weekly benefits` TIMES 25%)
        `the amount of the earnings, if any, that is greater than the threshold` MEANS
            max 0 (`the earnings of the claimant in the week, as determined for the purpose of subsection 19(2)` MINUS `the threshold`)
